<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Douglas, 5th Earl of Selkirk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1771">1771</a>–<a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lord Selkirk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Douglas, 5th Earl of Selkirk, was a Scottish peer who sponsored settlements of emigrant Highlanders in British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. In 1811 he obtained a huge land grant from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a>, which brought him into violent conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a>. He spent his last years in costly lawsuits over the colony and died in 1820.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-douglas-5th-earl-of-selkirk.jpg" alt="Thomas Douglas, 5th Earl of Selkirk" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas-douglas-fifth-earl-of-selkirk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
